  "decisions": {
    "lower_bpw_performance": "IQ2_XS/Q2_0 at about 2.29 expert bpw is the performance leader, not a penalty lane: at C8 it reached 35.18 tok/s trace-free versus 24.18 tok/s for MoESQ W4A8, with zero errors in both arms.",
    "short_read": "Default --short-read 64 wins over 128 and 256 for the batch-four high-cache workload; larger thresholds lowered throughput and worsened TTFT.",
    "batch_slots": "Eight slots improves C8 throughput from 34.01 to 35.18 tok/s trace-free (36.08 in the matching traced arm) at the cost of measured cache ratio 93.63% to 90.92%. Use batch 8 for throughput-oriented parallel agent tiers and batch 4 plus conversation parking when maximum measured cache ratio is preferred.",
    "prompt_cache": "Raising prompt-cache from 6 to 8 with eight slots did not recover cache ratio (90.87%), so the dip is not explained by checkpoint capacity.",
